---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import RelatedLinks from '../components/RelatedLinks.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { site, tel, sms, hoursText } from '../config/site';
import { page } from '../data/pages';
import { faqPage, service } from '../lib/schema';

const path = '/accountability-coaching/';
const meta = page(path);
const faqs = [
  { q: 'What does an accountability coach do?', a: "An accountability coach helps you set specific commitments and then checks that you did them. We agree on a few clear actions each week. Next session you report back: done, not done, and what got in the way. No shaming. We adjust the plan until it fits your real life, then we raise the bar a little." },
  { q: 'How is this different from an accountability partner or a buddy?', a: "A buddy is great, but buddies let things slide because they like you and don't want it to get awkward. I like you too, and I'll still ask the question. I also bring structure: a written plan, a weekly rhythm and a way to adjust when something keeps failing. That's harder to get from a friend." },
  { q: 'What if I miss a week or fall off completely?', a: "Then we talk about it, and we start again. Falling off is part of the process, not the end of it. Most of the useful work happens right after a slip, when we figure out what actually broke. The goal is not a perfect streak. The goal is getting back up faster each time." },
  { q: 'Can you help with discipline at the gym, with money or with drinking?', a: "Yes, coaching can help with the habits around all three: showing up to train, tracking spending, cutting back or quitting drinking. I am not a trainer, financial advisor or medical provider, so I won't write a workout or a budget. I help you decide what you'll do and then hold you to it." },
  { q: 'How many goals should I work on at once?', a: "Usually two or three, not ten. Men who try to fix everything at once burn out by week two. We pick the changes that make the rest easier, like sleep, a morning routine or one hard conversation. When those stick, we add more. Slow is faster than starting over every month." },
];
const schema = [
  service({ path, name: 'Accountability Coaching in Omaha', serviceType: 'Accountability coaching', description: meta.description }),
  faqPage(path, faqs),
];
---
<Base path={path} crumbs={[{ name: 'Accountability Coaching', path }]} schema={schema}>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Accountability coaching · Omaha" title="Accountability that holds on a bad Tuesday" lead="Monday you're all in. By Thursday the old habits are back. If that's your pattern, the problem isn't motivation. It's that nobody checks in." crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Accountability Coaching', path }]} updated={site.contentUpdated}>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn brass" href={site.booking} rel="noopener"><Icon name="calendar" />Book a Free Discovery Call</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href={sms}><Icon name="text" />Text Roland</a>
    </div>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="hook-h">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <h2 id="hook-h">What do you do on a bad Tuesday?</h2>
      <p>That's the first question I ask. Not what you'll do when you feel great. What you'll do when you slept four hours, your boss chewed you out and the kids are fighting in the back seat.</p>
      <p>Most plans are built for good days. They fall apart the first time life gets loud. Then you feel like a failure, so you quit, and three months later you start over with a new plan that also only works on good days.</p>
      <p>Accountability coaching breaks that loop. We build a plan with a floor, the bare minimum you'll do even on the worst day, and then someone actually asks how it went. Keep your word. Clean up your mess. Try again tomorrow.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section white" aria-labelledby="work-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">What we work on</p>
        <h2 id="work-h">Habits, discipline and keeping your word</h2>
        <p>We focus on the few habits that make everything else easier.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="card"><h3>Daily structure</h3><p>A morning and evening routine you can run half asleep. When the day has a shape, decisions get easier.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Consistency</h3><p>Training, eating, sleep, screen time. Smaller targets you actually hit beat big ones you abandon.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Self-sabotage</h3><p>Finding the moment you usually quit, and deciding ahead of time what you'll do instead.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Drinking and other habits</h3><p>Cutting back or stopping, with a plan for the nights it's hardest. Not a program. Your plan.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Work and money</h3><p>Following through on the job search, the side project, the budget you keep meaning to start.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Promises to people</h3><p>Calling when you said you would. Showing up on time. Trust comes back one kept promise at a time.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="sessions-h">
    <div class="wrap grid-2 top">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2 id="sessions-h">A weekly rhythm you can count on</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Free call.</strong> 20 minutes. What keeps happening, what you've tried, what you want.</li>
          <li><strong>Set the floor.</strong> In the first session we pick two or three commitments, each with a bad-day version.</li>
          <li><strong>Report back.</strong> Every session starts with the same question: did you do what you said? No lectures. Just the truth and the next step.</li>
          <li><strong>Adjust and raise.</strong> If something keeps failing, we change the plan. When it sticks, we add the next piece.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Sessions are in person in Omaha, by video or by phone. Here's how <a href="/omaha-life-coach/">coaching across Omaha</a> works, from meeting spots to the areas I serve. Hours: {hoursText}. Most men on accountability coaching pick <a href="/pricing/">Core Coaching at $249 a month</a> for weekly sessions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark grain" aria-labelledby="change-h">
    <div class="wrap grid-2 top">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What changes</p>
        <h2 id="change-h">Keeping your word becomes normal again</h2>
        <p>No guarantees. The work is yours. But here's what tends to happen when men stop starting over:</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>You stop restarting every Monday because you never fully quit.</li>
        <li>Slips get shorter. One bad day stays one bad day.</li>
        <li>You trust yourself again, because you've watched yourself follow through.</li>
        <li>The people around you notice you do what you say.</li>
        <li>Discipline stops feeling like punishment and starts feeling like relief.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="not-h">
    <div class="wrap grid-2 top">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Honest fit</p><h2 id="not-h">Who this is not for</h2></div>
      <div class="prose">
        <ul class="x-list">
          <li>Men who want to be yelled at. That's not how I work. I'm direct, not a drill sergeant.</li>
          <li>Men who want me to do the work for them.</li>
          <li data-scope>Anyone who needs medical detox, medication management, therapy or crisis care. Coaching can work alongside that support but does not replace it.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If you're not sure, <a href={tel}>call {site.phone.display}</a> and ask. I'll tell you straight.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section white" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2 id="faq-h">Accountability coaching questions</h2></div>
      <Faq faqs={faqs} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <RelatedLinks heading="Related coaching" links={[
    { href: '/mens-life-coaching-omaha/', title: "Men's life coaching in Omaha", text: 'The bigger picture: direction, structure and confidence for men who feel stuck.' },
    { href: '/rebuilding-after-addiction/', title: 'Rebuilding after addiction', text: 'Routine, accountability and rebuilding trust, from someone who has lived it.' },
    { href: '/blog/what-to-do-on-a-bad-tuesday/', title: 'What to do on a bad Tuesday', text: 'A simple plan for the days motivation disappears. Read the post.' },
  ]} />
</Base>
